There are several ways to terminate a C program:

1. Using the return statement:

The most common way to terminate a C program is by using the return statement. You can use the return statement with a value or without it. If you use it without a value, it will return 0 by default.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    return 0;
}
```

2. Using the exit() function:

Another way to terminate a C program is by using the exit() function. This function takes an integer argument that represents the exit status of the program.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    exit(0);
}
```

3. Using the return keyword with an expression:

You can also use the return keyword with an expression to terminate the program and return a value.

